WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.468
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.137
to another edition
of "Late Night"

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.072
in a makeshift home studio.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.641
And as you can see, we're
trying yet another location

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.909
in my house.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.911
We had been shooting
in a garage,

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.380
but we abandoned that
because it was so cold

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.282
that by the end of Monday's
"Closer Look,"

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.919
my nose was redder
than a cartoon drunk.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.687
I mean, look at that thing.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:24.557
It was like
"Late Night with Andy Capp."

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.993
No, I never would have made
an Andy Capp reference

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.761
in front of a live audience
because silence

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.062
would have been deafening,

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.798
but these days that's
the reaction to everything.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.568
So I figured, you know,
why not let it rip?

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.637
So today we're giving it a shot
from a crawl space in the attic,

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.240
and when I told my 4-year-old
Daddy was going up to the attic

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.175
for a while, he said
the cutest thing.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:46.713
"If you and Mom are getting
a divorce, just tell us."

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.147
Kids, right?

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.115
And it looks like I'll be doing
these shows from home

00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:52.552
for a while now that
the president has extended

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.254
the social distancing guidelines
to the end of April

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.356
while he and allies try
to memory-hole

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.792
their early dismissal
of the coronavirus outbreak.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:02.795
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:06.566
♪♪

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.168
Donald Trump has tried
repeatedly to claim

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.871
that no one could have seen
this crisis coming,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.173
even though he was
repeatedly warned

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.375
in intelligence briefings
in January and February

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:17.810
that it was coming.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.779
In fact, the "New York Times"
reported Tuesday

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.515
that White House economists
published a study

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.217
last September that warned
a pandemic disease could kill

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:28.287
a half million Americans
and devastate the economy.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:31.090
It went unheeded inside
the administration.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.392
"Unheeded" is a generous
description.

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:35.562
In reality, what probably
happened was an economist

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.697
put the study
on Trump's desk and said,

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.998
"Sir, you should read this,"

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.433
and he said,
"What is it, nerd?"

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.534
And then the economist said,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.236
"It's about a possible
pandemic."

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.271
And Trump said,
"What's a pandemic, Poindexter?"

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.639
And then the economist said,

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.674
"A pandemic is when
a disease spreads,"

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:51.244
and before he could finish,
Trump was asleep on his desk

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:54.714
with a Burger King wrapper
stuck to his face.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.048
Probably.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.484
And of course it went unheeded.
Trump doesn't heed.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.221
He doesn't heed the law.
He doesn't heed advice.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.990
And he especially doesn't
heed studies.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.292
In fact, he makes it
actively harder

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.994
for everyone else
to heed studies.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.330
For example, at his press
conference Tuesday night,

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.866
he turned the mic over
to task force coordinator

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.769
Dr. Deborah Birx, who took
the room of reporters

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.472
through a series of important
slides of valuable data,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.440
and Trump just wandered over

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.643
and stood right in front
of the screen.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.978
"Hey, man, we're trying to read.
Get out of the way."

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:27.813
"Should I stand right here
in front of the screen

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.215
so you can't read it?

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.251
Is that helpful, Dr. Birx?
Dr. Birx?

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.252
Maybe I'll stand in front of the
part that represents the time

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.187
I should have done something
when I didn't do anything?

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:36.522
What do you think, Fauci?

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:39.491
Oh, oh, I got you again, Fauci.

00:02:39.491 --> 00:02:41.594
I got you to touch
your face again.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:45.631
Oh, this is my favorite game,
Fauci, and I always win.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.500
I'm just kidding, we're pals.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.869
Trump and Fauci,
the original Lenny and Squiggy.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.770
That's what people say."

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.205
Seriously, man, the only reason

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.907
anyone tunes in to
these briefings

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.642
is to hear the
scientists.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.178
They're the feature
presentation.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:02.014
You're a dancing box of popcorn
singing --

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:04.651
♪ Let's go out to the lobby ♪

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:07.053
♪ Let's go out
to the lobby ♪

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.021
♪ Let's go out to the lobby ♪

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.124
♪ And ignore this
terrifying data ♪

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.793
And that wasn't the only warning
the Trump administration got.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.428
In fact, before Trump
even took office,

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.563
President Obama's outgoing team
tried to prepare Trump

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:20.366
and his aides for a scenario
exactly like this one.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.301
-Days before Donald Trump
took office,

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.070
some of President Obama's
advisers

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.071
walked the incoming
president's team

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:28.841
through a hypothetical scenario
remarkably like the one

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.543
we're living through now.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.212
It was a briefing on what would
happen if a quick-spreading

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:36.048
virus were to race through
London and Seoul,

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.450
and in that scenario
they presented governments

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.986
imposing travel bans,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.121
there were shortages at
hospitals across the country,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.624
and today, roughly two-thirds of
those Trump administration

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:48.394
officials who participated
in that simulation

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.197
are no longer in government.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.765
-Of course they aren't.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.167
This administration runs through
employees faster

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.137
than an ice cream shop
on the Coney Island Boardwalk.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.473
Someone should have run
a simulation for what happens

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.642
when an egomaniac fires
every staff member

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.310
who ever disagrees with him.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.612
"After three years,
the simulation does show

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:09.349
it will be down to you,
a professional liar,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.018
and a Victorian-era
teenage ghost."

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.520
I mean, Trump has had four,
four Chiefs of Staff

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.889
in four years, and the current
one, Mark Meadows,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.757
officially started
on the job yesterday.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:21.093
Man, what a time to start
working for this White House.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.062
"All right, show me
to my new office."

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.598
"I can't, it's been turned
into a field hospital.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.433
Also, you're the
surgeon general now."

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.202
And what's his next move,
zookeeper

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.504
at Joe Exotic's animal park?

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.240
And even if the officials
in that briefing were still

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.076
in government, I bet they didn't
learn anything anyway

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.712
because Trump was standing
directly in front of the screen.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.847
So Trump had many warnings

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.483
that something like this
was coming,

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:46.418
and yet he and his aides
repeatedly downplayed

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.321
or dismissed the threat.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.290
He said cases would
go down to zero,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.658
that it would miraculously
disappear,

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:55.695
and compared it to the flu
even though coronavirus

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:59.065
is much more infectious
and much deadlier.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.633
-This is a flu.
This is like a flu.

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:03.202
You treat this like a flu.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:06.572
It's a little like the regular
flu that we have flu shots for.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.640
And we'll essentially have
a flu shot for this

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.208
in a fairly quick manner.

00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:12.277
The flu in our country

00:05:12.277 --> 00:05:18.017
kills from 25,000 people
to 69,000 people a year.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.718
That was shocking to me.

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:23.355
Over the last ten years,
we've lost 360,000.

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:25.991
These are people
that have died from the flu,

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.493
from what we call the flu.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.862
-What do you mean,
what we call the flu?

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.330
It's the flu.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.432
We all call it the flu.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:34.967
Trump talks about regular words

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.802
like they're complicated
medical jargon.

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.737
"We in the scientific community
call it the flu.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:41.640
It's called that because it
started over in Europe

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.243
and then it flew here."

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.578
Also basically everything he
said in that clip was wrong.

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.814
Turns out you aren't
an expert in science

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:51.217
just because you look like
a science experiment.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.085
He's like a bunch of body parts
a dead gangster

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:54.620
has sewn together
and brought to life

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.223
by a guy who went to school
with Dr. Frankenstein

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.958
but dropped out
sophomore year.

00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:02.494
I can just see him
being tormented by villagers

00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:04.764
with torches --
"Ah, fire bad,

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:07.800
but not that bad, basically
the same as the flu.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.668
Ah!"

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.871
Trump should be in a documentary
where Jane Goodall

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.439
teaches him
sign language.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:16.742
"Donald, can you say the words
'distribution emergency'?"

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.744
-Distribution<i> evergency.</i>

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:21.680
-And then less than a month ago,
Trump tweeted,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.251
"So last year 37,000 Americans
died from the common flu.

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:29.488
It averages between 27,000
and 70,000 per year.

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:30.857
Nothing is shut down.

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.124
Life and the economy go on.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:34.726
At this moment there are
546 confirmed cases

00:06:34.726 --> 00:06:37.096
of coronavirus
with 22 deaths.

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.764
Think about that."

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:41.466
Any time a world-renowned idiot
like Donald Trump

00:06:41.466 --> 00:06:43.268
tells you to think about that,
that's your cue

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.071
to exit the conversation.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.373
He's like the dumbest guy
at a cocktail party

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.174
trying to make conversation
by telling you

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:51.010
something he read
on a Snapple cap.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:54.013
"Broccoli, you know, only
vegetable that's also a flower,

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:56.548
so, that's something
to think about."

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:58.951
Of course, the lie that
coronavirus is just like the flu

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.519
did obvious damage.

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:03.489
You know how many people heard
that and then repeated it?

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.090
Even if you hated Donald Trump

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.226
and knew not to trust
a word he said,

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:10.129
everyone had
that one friend or relative

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.597
