00:10:25.191 --> 00:10:28.193
"This is not Jeffrey Dahmer
the crazed murderer.

00:10:28.193 --> 00:10:30.128
This was a more serious Dahmer,

00:10:30.128 --> 00:10:34.166
just quietly home-cooking
a meal for one."

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:35.734
Of course it was a different
Donald Trump.

00:10:35.734 --> 00:10:37.636
It's a different Donald Trump
every night, which means

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:39.337
it's always the same
Donald Trump.

00:10:39.337 --> 00:10:41.907
He never fundamentally changes
who he is as a person.

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.009
He just swings wildly
back and forth

00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:45.877
from one extreme
to the other.

00:10:45.877 --> 00:10:50.182
He's like a werewolf but for
the sun instead of the moon.

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:53.785
But Trump isn't the only one
trying to memory-hole

00:10:53.785 --> 00:10:56.088
his initial response
to the crisis.

00:10:56.088 --> 00:10:59.691
There's also one of his closest
and most loyal defenders on TV,

00:10:59.691 --> 00:11:01.126
Sean Hannity.

00:11:01.126 --> 00:11:03.228
A few weeks ago,
Hannity tried to claim

00:11:03.228 --> 00:11:05.530
he was taking the
situation seriously.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:08.634
And on Monday he actually
accused others in the media

00:11:08.634 --> 00:11:10.702
of spreading
conspiracy theories.

00:11:10.702 --> 00:11:13.406
-This program has always taken
the coronavirus seriously.

00:11:13.406 --> 00:11:16.074
And we've never called
the virus a hoax.

00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:19.778
How does anyone trust the
outright conspiracy theorists,

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:23.282
that whole network full of lies,
conspiracy theories?

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:25.985
-Dude, all you do is
spread conspiracy theories.

00:11:25.985 --> 00:11:28.320
You're like Alex Jones without
the brain pills.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.155
In fact, you should probably
take some.

00:11:30.155 --> 00:11:31.990
Your network spent years
promoting

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:34.259
insane conspiracy theories
from death panels

00:11:34.259 --> 00:11:37.763
to birtherism to
nonexistent voter fraud.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:41.734
Fox has even interviewed
an actual lizard person.

00:11:44.069 --> 00:11:46.304
And in particular,
in this particular case,

00:11:46.304 --> 00:11:48.941
Hannity lined up behind Trump
during his early claim

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:50.909
that the coronavirus
was no big deal,

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:53.178
using the word "hoax"
to describe criticism

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:55.781
of Trump's response
and even suggesting at one point

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:59.051
that it might be a deep-state
plot to destroy the economy.

00:11:59.051 --> 00:12:01.320
-They are now sadly
politicizing and actually

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.056
weaponizing an infectious
disease,

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:06.325
in what is basically
just the latest effort

00:12:06.325 --> 00:12:08.193
to bludgeon President Trump.

00:12:08.193 --> 00:12:10.229
They're scaring the living hell
out of people.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:12.031
And I see it again as, like,

00:12:12.031 --> 00:12:14.733
"Oh, let's bludgeon Trump
with this new hoax."

00:12:14.733 --> 00:12:18.370
There's an MIT guy I noticed
on Twitter, he said, quote,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.473
"Coronavirus fearmongering
by the deep state will go down

00:12:21.473 --> 00:12:25.243
in history as one of the biggest
frauds to manipulate economies,

00:12:25.243 --> 00:12:29.415
suppress dissent, and push
mandated medicines."

00:12:29.415 --> 00:12:31.116
May be true.

00:12:31.116 --> 00:12:34.186
-You're not a news show
if you end your segment

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:35.921
with "May be true."

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:37.856
That's a tagline
you get at 2:00 A.M.

00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:39.625
after one of those shows
about ancient aliens

00:12:39.625 --> 00:12:41.426
teaching the Aztecs
how to grow grain.

00:12:41.426 --> 00:12:44.529
"May be true.
Probably bull [bleep]."

00:12:44.529 --> 00:12:46.232
Seriously, we should get
Trump in there

00:12:46.232 --> 00:12:48.967
to stand in front of
Hannity during a show.

00:12:48.967 --> 00:12:52.938
So one more time, side by side,
here is Sean Hannity.

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:55.140
-They're scaring the living
hell out of people,

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.842
and I see it again as like,

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:59.611
"Oh, let's bludgeon Trump
with this new hoax."

00:12:59.611 --> 00:13:02.581
This program has always taken
the coronavirus seriously

00:13:02.581 --> 00:13:05.150
and we've never called the virus
a hoax.

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.218
-Man, that takes some balls.

00:13:07.218 --> 00:13:09.621
If Donald Trump turned out to be
an incredible president

00:13:09.621 --> 00:13:11.690
who brought the country
together, I'd eat my words.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.758
I wouldn't sit here and swear

00:13:13.758 --> 00:13:16.662
that I never once said
he should be in a documentary

00:13:16.662 --> 00:13:19.198
where Jane Goodall teaches him
sign language.

00:13:19.198 --> 00:13:20.933
Trump should be in a documentary

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.202
where Jane Goodall
teaches him sign language.

00:13:23.202 --> 00:13:27.172
No, sure, I mean, yeah, when you
cut it together like that.

00:13:27.172 --> 00:13:29.841
The president and his allies
wasted precious weeks

00:13:29.841 --> 00:13:31.876
when we could have been
preparing for this crisis.

00:13:31.876 --> 00:13:33.912
We saw it coming.
We could have ramped up testing

00:13:33.912 --> 00:13:36.247
and hospital capacity,
quarantined and traced cases

00:13:36.247 --> 00:13:37.649
to contain the spread.

00:13:37.649 --> 00:13:40.619
Now we're facing the prospect
of a horrible tragedy.

00:13:40.619 --> 00:13:42.454
And when the time for
accountability comes,

00:13:42.454 --> 00:13:44.222
Trump should be removed
from office...

00:13:44.222 --> 00:13:45.824
-In a fairly quick manner.

00:13:45.824 --> 00:13:47.192
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:47.192 --> 00:13:50.362
♪♪

00:13:50.362 --> 00:13:53.032
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

